WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.560
Every Chola bronze begins as

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.430
beeswax. And the wax is lost.

3
00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:07.147
An ancient craft.

4
00:00:07.147 --> 00:00:10.707
NCERT says the lost wax method

5
00:00:10.707 --> 00:00:12.947
was known in the Indus Valley.

6
00:00:12.947 --> 00:00:14.867
The Dancing Girl of Mohenjo

7
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:16.667
daro, about twenty five hundred

8
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:19.427
BCE, is perhaps the earliest

9
00:00:19.427 --> 00:00:20.717
bronze sculpture.

10
00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:22.327
First, wax.

11
00:00:22.327 --> 00:00:25.167
Pure beeswax is melted, strained

12
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.407
through cloth into cold water,

13
00:00:27.407 --> 00:00:29.187
pressed into noodle like wires,

14
00:00:29.187 --> 00:00:31.207
and wound into the shape of the

15
00:00:31.207 --> 00:00:32.007
image.

16
00:00:32.663 --> 00:00:34.243
Then, clay.

17
00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:36.803
The wax image gets a thick coat

18
00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.603
of clay, sand and cow dung, with

19
00:00:39.603 --> 00:00:41.543
an opening on one side for a

20
00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:42.493
clay pot.

21
00:00:43.431 --> 00:00:45.311
Fire, then pour.

22
00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.871
Heat melts the wax out, and

23
00:00:47.871 --> 00:00:50.211
molten metal, ten times the wax

24
00:00:50.211 --> 00:00:52.251
in weight, takes its place.

25
00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.731
Often it is scrap from old pots

26
00:00:54.731 --> 00:00:55.831
and pans.

27
00:00:55.831 --> 00:00:57.581
The original recycling.

28
00:00:58.245 --> 00:00:59.465
Finally, file.

29
00:00:59.465 --> 00:01:02.165
The cast image is chiselled and

30
00:01:02.165 --> 00:01:03.025
filed smooth.

31
00:01:03.025 --> 00:01:06.065
NCERT calls it painstaking work,

32
00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.835
needing great skill.

33
00:01:08.322 --> 00:01:09.582
The Chola peak.

34
00:01:09.582 --> 00:01:12.002
Tamil Nadu, tenth to twelfth

35
00:01:12.002 --> 00:01:14.402
century. The dancing Nataraja

36
00:01:14.402 --> 00:01:16.422
form was fully developed then.

37
00:01:16.422 --> 00:01:18.762
Kumbakonam still keeps the craft

38
00:01:18.762 --> 00:01:19.562
alive.

39
00:01:20.818 --> 00:01:21.545
For GS1:

40
00:01:21.545 --> 00:01:23.338
the lost wax process, also

41
00:01:23.338 --> 00:01:25.198
called cire perdu;

42
00:01:25.198 --> 00:01:28.298
Chola bronzes of the tenth to

43
00:01:28.298 --> 00:01:28.898
twelfth century;

44
00:01:28.898 --> 00:01:30.658
the Nataraja form;

45
00:01:30.658 --> 00:01:33.791
patron Queen Sembiyan Maha Devi.

46
00:01:34.473 --> 00:01:36.573
The wax is lost.

47
00:01:36.573 --> 00:01:38.043
The image remains.
